# Generated per run. Both hold PRODUCTION catalog content — row bodies, uuids, curator
# rulings — which is why they stay out of the repo, the same reason
# scripts/ops/2026-09-stranded-row-audit/ gitignores its report and id list.
#
# The earlier one-row retraction lanes DO commit their rollback.sql, and that was right for
# a lane that ran once against three rows. This one is re-runnable and its rollback carries
# the whole feed, so the same choice would mean committing a few hundred KB of catalog rows
# on every run.
#
# KEEP THE ROLLBACK SOMEWHERE. It is the statement-level undo and it is not in git. The
# database-level backstop is Cloudflare D1 Time Travel (30 days, whole database); attach the
# file to the issue, or record its Time Travel bookmark, before the window closes. See the
# README's account of the run that lost one.
preflight-*.json
rollback-*.sql
